# Written against the Homebrew npm (/opt/homebrew/opt/node/bin/npm). npm 12
# differs: 12.2.0 drops adduser, shrinkwrap, star, stars, unstar and the
# add-user alias, and adds patch; regenerate from that package root to follow it.
#
# Generated from the installed package (lib/utils/cmd-list.js, the command
# classes under lib/commands/, and @npmcli/config's definitions and shorthands),
# then checked against `npm <command> --help` for every command and stage/trust
# subcommand. Per-command positionals and the subcommand tables are written by
# hand from each command's usage and exec() switch.
#
# An option is shown plainly where `npm <command> --help` prints it, and marked
# "(hidden)" everywhere else. `-h` is plain everywhere and `-l` at the root,
# because the root usage documents both. A short form the command's help leaves
# out is hidden even when its long form is printed (`-D` on install).
#
# Hidden surface, every item confirmed against npm itself:
#   * Config options: every config key is accepted as `--key` by every command
#     (npm warns `Unknown cli config "--x"` for anything else), but each
#     command's help prints only its own params.
#   * `--no-<key>` for every boolean config key.
#   * Shorthands from the config shorthands table: -d, -q, -s, --quiet,
#     --silent, --verbose, --dd, --ddd (loglevel presets), --enjoy-by, --desc,
#     --help, --iwr, --local, -n, --no, --porcelain, --readonly, --reg, --ws,
#     -?, -H.
#   * Deprecated config keys: also, cache-max, cache-min, cert, dev,
#     global-style, init.author.email, init.author.name, init.author.url,
#     init.license, init.module, init.version, key, legacy-bundling, only,
#     optional, production, shrinkwrap.
#   * trust github/gitlab/circleci/list/revoke: `--no-<flag>` for each of their
#     own boolean options. Their own options (--file, --repository, --id, ...)
#     exist only under trust and are scoped there.
#   * Subcommand aliases from the exec() switches: cache rm, clear (clean) and
#     check (verify); config rm, del (delete) and ls (list); dist-tag a, set, s
#     (add), r, del, d, remove (rm) and l, sl, list (ls); install-scripts list
#     (ls); org add (set); owner list (ls) and remove (rm); profile enable-tfa,
#     enable2fa, enabletfa, disable-tfa, disable2fa, disabletfa; token ls
#     (list) and rm, delete, remove (revoke).
#   * Values: access set 2fa=none|publish|automation (same as mfa=), doctor
#     ping (same check group as connection).
#
# Command aliases are listed by each command's own --help, so they are not
# marked. Dispatched but deliberately not offered:
#   * The misspellings innit, isnt, isnta, isntal, isntall, isntall-clean, hlep,
#     udpate, rum, urn, ogr, sit and verison, and the pinned prefixes of install
#     in, ins, inst, insta and instal.
#   * Unique prefixes of command names (`npm conf get`): npm resolves them, and
#     so does this file when dispatching, but they are not offered.
# Not completed at all:
#   * Prefixes of option names (`--par` for --parseable) and single-dash spellings
#     of multi-letter shorthands (`-dd`, `-ws`, `-iwr`), which npm warns it will
#     stop accepting.
#   * `access ls`: npm's own completion offers it, but `npm access ls` fails with
#     "ls is not a valid access command".
#   * `trust gitlab --repo/--repository`: printed in that command's usage line,
#     rejected by its parser ("Unknown flags: --repo").
#   * Field names for `npm view <pkg> <field>` and package lists for deprecate
#     and unpublish: npm completes these with a registry round-trip.
#   * npx, which is a separate executable.
#
# Dynamic values are read locally: installed packages from node_modules (with
# -g, from `npm root -g`), scripts, package.json fields and workspaces through
# node, and help topics from npm's own man pages.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

